[As usual, I was playing on my Zaurus. For those who haven't seen the PDA
version of nethack, the map, status, and log are on separate screens.
Messages are superimposed on the screen at each turn, but disappear at the
next screentap or keypress, after which you have to read the log if you
weren't paying attention or want to scroll to see what all that cookie
said.]

In minetown, I wound up pinned in Izchak's shop by all these gnomes who
wanted to talk with me. After taking care of the last wizard I'd hoped to
see for a while, all I wanted to do was relax and chat with the shopkeeper
about this lamp he had sitting there. Unfortunately, I didn't notice among
all the fighting that I'd been stunned somehow. So of course, the first
move I made toward the lamp was instead interpreted badly by the RGN and
rudely by Izchak. 

Obviously, before making another move, I should have tabbed over and
looked at my status window or log. That way I would have know that resting
in place would have been a good idea for a while.


